  "question": {
    "text": "A particle is projected vertically upwards. If it has to stay above the ground for 12 seconds, then"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "velocity of projection is $192 \\mathrm{ft} / \\mathrm{sec}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "greatest height attained is $600 \\mathrm{ft}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "velocity of projection is $196 \\mathrm{ft} / \\mathrm{sec}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "greatest height attained is $576 \\mathrm{ft}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A",
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint:\r\n$V=u-g t$ at $t=6$\r\n$u-g t=0$\r\n$\\Rightarrow u=6 g=192 f t /$ sec $\\quad\\left(g=32 f t / \\sec ^{2}\\right) \\ldots \\ldots . .(\\mathrm{i})$\r\n$x=u t=\\frac{1}{2} g t^{2}$\r\n$=192.6-\\frac{1}{2} 32.6^{2}$\r\n$=576 \\mathrm{ft}$"
  }
}